s/proxy.json path the sole acceptance criterion greps for. The failure is purely that the attempt ended dirty rather than committed. One live boundary hazard explains why a naive \"git add -A\" would fail again: the untracked path results/receipts/proxy.json is a runtime receipt emitted by an actual serve run and is NOT inside any conflict domain, so committing it would make the same conflict-domains gate fail for the opposite reason. Attempt 2 steering: 1) Preserve the three existing in-domain files as they are; re-derive nothing and do not rewrite the scripts wholesale — this is a stateless reconcile over work already present in the lane. 2) Remove the out-of-domain artifact results/receipts/proxy.json from the worktree before committing (it is disposable runtime output that scripts/run-proxy.sh regenerates), so the tree is clean and no commit touches a path outside the domains. Do not add it to .gitignore or any other file, since those paths are also out of domain. 3) Stage exactly scripts/make-proxy.sh, scripts/run-proxy.sh, and tests/test_proxy_tooling.py — nothing else — and commit on the assigned branch tally-work/flashnext-cac9adc5400c/proxy-tooling. Do not push or merge. 4) Before committing, self-check the acceptance criterion locally: bash -n scripts/make-proxy.sh scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -q 'results/receipts/proxy.json' scripts/run-proxy.sh. 5) After the commit, verify with git status --porcelain that the tree is empty and with git show --stat that every path in the commit begins with scripts/make-proxy.sh, scripts/run-proxy.sh, or tests/. 6) Return the final result envelope as the last message so the adapter's finalMessage capture projects instead of timing out. Note for the record, not for fixing here: the receipt from the attempted run recorded status fail with an engine-core OOM during boot and an amdsmi absence in the container. Those are pair-lane and fork-lane concerns outside this task's authorized paths and outside its single acceptance criterion; attempt 2 must not chase them and must not widen scope to make a live serve pass.","taskId":"proxy-tooling","verdict":"retry"}],"retries":[],"outcomes":[],"deferrals":[{"taskId":"cp-weights","waitingOn":["proxy-tooling","morning-ledger","catalog-handoff","rdma-package"]},{"taskId":"cp-build","waitingOn":["proxy-tooling","morning-ledger","catalog-handoff","rdma-package"]},{"taskId":"cp-smoke","waitingOn":["proxy-tooling","morning-ledger","catalog-handoff","rdma-package"]},{"taskId":"cp-proxy","waitingOn":["morning-ledger","catalog-handoff","rdma-package"]},{"taskId":"cp-tp2","waitingOn":["morning-ledger","catalog-handoff","rdma-package"]},{"taskId":"cp-bench","waitingOn":["morning-ledger","catalog-handoff","rdma-package"]},{"taskId":"cp-close","waitingOn":["rdma-package"]}],"blocked":[],"quiescent":false,"escalation":null,"closingSummary":null,"warnings":[]},"maintenance":{"blockingJobs":[],"cleaned":["pass:/home/tom/.local/state/tally/campaigns/flashnext/.state/passes/cac9adc5400c.json"],"currentRunHash":"667bc3eb0212","liveRuns":[],"warnings":[]},"checkpoints":[],"merged":[],"published":null,"failures":[{"taskId":"proxy-tooling","stage":"ownership","verdict":"failed","detail":"{\"code\":\"result-schema-mismatch\",\"message\":\"configured finalMessage capture for adapter \\\"spec-build-driver\\\" was not projected within 10000 ms\",\"details\":{\"projection\":{\"code\":\"result-projection-timeout\",\"message\":\"configured finalMessage capture for adapter \\\"spec-build-driver\\\" was not projected within 10000 ms\",\"details\":{\"adapter\":\"spec-build-driver\",\"attempt\":1,\"taskUuid\":\"01a04d0f-bc52-73f1-93f0-e566a9e05c17\",\"timeoutMs\":10000,\"exitEvidencePassed\":false}}}}"}],"diagnoses":[{"attempt":2,"blocked":true,"comment":"local://campaign/flashnext/attempt-receipts/4","kind":"diagnosis","posted":true,"redacted":false,"retry":null,"taskId":"proxy-tooling","verdict":"blocked"}],"retries":[],"outcomes":[],"deferrals":[],"continuation":{"created":tru